    "created_at": "2018-09-11T10:17:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-11T10:17:56Z",
    "body": "The legend is constrained by the content box inline size established by the fieldset, while it obviously ignores block-start padding?\r\n\r\nIt's still unclear to me how padding works here, though. It's said to set the used value of all sides to 0 on the fieldset container, while it's inherited to the inner fieldset contents anonymous box. But how can we resolve percentage padding then?\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div style=\"width:500px;\">\r\n  <fieldset style=\"width:100px; border:10px solid; padding:10%;\">\r\n    <legend>...</legend>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe legend's left border edge, relatively to the left border edge of the fieldset, should be at 60px (10px border plus 10% of 500px as padding).\r\nThe fieldset should get a padding of 50px on each side. But how's that supposed to happen, when we in reality have this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div style=\"width:500px;\">\r\n  <fieldset style=\"width:100px; border:10px solid;\">\r\n    <legend>...</legend>\r\n    <anon id=\"fieldset-content\" style=\"display:block; padding:10%;\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe containing block of #fieldset-content is fieldset, and the width of the containing block established by that one is 100px, while we really ought to resolve the percentages against the div (500px).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/420222937/reactions",
