    "created_at": "2018-09-11T10:33:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-11T10:33:51Z",
    "body": "I wonder if it would be helpful to spec the FIELDSET/LEGEND box model more similarly to how it's done for a table and its table wrapper box:\r\n\r\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/CSS22/tables.html#model\r\n\r\nI.e. avoid the concept of an anonymous box entirely, since there's clearly more to it than what can be expressed with that solution.\r\n\r\nWe could say that there's a fieldset wrapper container, which contains the rendered legend and the fieldset contents box. Then define which properties apply to which box (padding, column-count, overflow, etc. on the contents box; the remaining properties on the container box).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/420227456/reactions",
