    "body": "From @bzbarsky:\r\n\r\n> When Gecko is setting up the layout for the fieldset content container, it explicitly gives it the fieldset’s “computed” (not sure this matches the CSS concept of “computed” or “used” per se) padding to use instead of whatever the container computed for itself.  See  https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/9e7995b3c384945740985107a4de601b27904718/layout/forms/nsFieldSetFrame.cpp#484-486\r\n",
